group degrees: the quantitative toolkit","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:5a6339d246521e4a19eacab33dc963accbf13c536db9d04b8fe971e0c14ae2f6","file":"preprints/From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026/build/sections/degrees.tex","line":162,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"913168536ce740ba96dde5f5ffd2df835194adcfcd73444097b7424fde2d945d","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026/build/sections/degrees.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5a6339d246521e4a19eacab33dc963accbf13c536db9d04b8fe971e0c14ae2f6","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/From-partial-permutation-information-to-Fourier-bounds-September-26-2026/build/sections/degrees.tex#L162"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{l:degree-all-powers}\nFor every fixed real $u>0$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{l:degree-all-powers-equation}\n C_u:=\\sup_{n\\ge1}\\sum_{\\lambda\\vdash n}D_\\lambda^{-u}<\\infty,\n \\qquad Z_u(n)\\longrightarrow0.\n\\end{equation}\nMoreover there are absolute constants $c_1,c_2>0$ such that, for all\nsufficiently large $n$ and every $\\lambda\\vdash n$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{l:degree-tail-exponential}\n D_\\lambda\\ge c_1e^{c_2k(\\lambda)}.\n\\end{equation}\nFor each fixed positive $k$, these dimensions tend uniformly to infinity\namong shapes with $k(\\lambda)=k$."}
